  Leather armor is lightweight and spell friendly.  Spell friendly
body armor is critical for spell casters, because it takes so long to
take off and wear.  +3 leather armor gives as much protection as elven
mithril, weighs the same, and is spell friendly.  

  That's why I generally check all the leather armor dropped by dead
leather golems.  I've found up to +4 before.  That's the next best
thing to dragon scale mail.

  If it's not dragon scale mail only spell friendliness and total AC
improvement matter.  You're not going to enchant it further since it's
not DSM.

